<title>SOUTH AFRICA: I&amp;J HALF YEAR EARNINGS PER SHR RISES.</title>
<headline>I&amp;J HALF YEAR EARNINGS PER SHR RISES.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Pre-excep shr, attrib (cts)   15.9	vs 10.7</p>
<p>    Post-excep shr (cts)	    14.8	vs 10.1</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			     55.62     vs 37.14</p>
<p>    Tax				   12.95     vs  8.07</p>
<p>    Interest paid		     13.57     vs 10.30</p>
<p>    Turnover			 1,286.3	vs 1,080.16</p>
<p>    Exceptional items		  3.22 paid   vs 1.83 paid</p>
<p>Full name: Irvin &amp; Johnson Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Food group Irvin &amp; Johnson Ltd said it had paid</p>
<p>dividends worth 28.91 million rand in the period, compared to</p>
<p>28.80 million rand last time.</p>
<p>The firm added that, despite dificult local trading</p>
<p>conditions, it anticipated its year profit would show growth</p>
<p>over the comparable period.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
